==============================================================================
PHASE 6 — A DAY-LONG ADVANCE, and the halts do not fire SPURIOUSLY
==============================================================================
The bullet a suite skips. An unconditional halt that fires on nothing
is a wedge, and 'it did not halt' is unprovable on a live colony — so
'not spurious' is given a testable meaning: EVERY halt must name a
journal row that EXISTS, of the matching type, at the seq it
published. A halt with nothing behind it is the failure.

Budget: 60000 ticks (1.00 in-game days). Use --day-ticks to shorten.
